    "description": "Progress test 1 10.0%",
    "content": "<div class=\"ml-en\"><span class=\"eyebrow\">HOA102 · Assessment 5/7</span>\n<h2>Progress test 1</h2>\n<p class=\"nhan\">Source: FLM syllabus 13352 · assessment table (verbatim)</p></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><span class=\"eyebrow\">HOA102 · Đầu điểm 5/7</span>\n<h2>Progress test 1</h2>\n<p class=\"nhan\">Nguồn: syllabus FLM 13352 · bảng đánh giá (nguyên văn)</p></div>\n<div class=\"kv-grid\">\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">Type / Loại</span><span class=\"v\">on-going</span></div>\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">Weight / Trọng số</span><span class=\"v\">10.0%</span></div>\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">Parts / Số phần</span><span class=\"v\">1</span></div>\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">Completion criteria / Điều kiện hoàn thành</span><span class=\"v\">&gt;0</span></div>\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">Duration / Thời lượng</span><span class=\"v\">Option 1: Week 5 in class Option 2: (For Constructivism Approach only): Follow lecturer's proposal</span></div>\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">CLO</span><span class=\"v\">LO2, LO3, LO4</span></div>\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">Question type / Dạng câu hỏi</span><span class=\"v\">Option 1: Research-based &amp; Applied Assignment<br>Option 2: (For Constructivism Approach only): Follow lecturer's</span></div>\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">No. of questions / Số câu</span><span class=\"v\">Option 1: 1; Opttion 2: 1; Option 3: (For Constructivism Approach only): Follow lecturer's proposal</span></div>\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">Knowledge &amp; skill / Kiến thức &amp; kỹ năng</span><span class=\"v\">Chapter I-VIII/ Part 1</span></div>\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">Grading guide / Hướng dẫn chấm</span><span class=\"v\">Option 1: 'Option 1: Individual exercise<br>Each student chooses a 20th-century art Style (e.g., Cubism, Surrealism, Abstract Expressionism, Pop Art, etc.). Then, take inspiration from the chosen style to create a new artwork (digital or hand-drawn).<br><br>Notes/Requirements:<br>- Explain the characteristics of the style: Describe the key characteristics, techniques, themes, and visual elements of the chosen style.<br>- Analyze your creative process: Clarify how you applied the chosen style to your work (e.g., composition, use of color, symbolism, technique).<br>- Use of AI-assisted tools is allowed: You may use AI to assist your creative process (e.g., creating references, visualizing concepts, experimenting with composition), but the final work must reflect your originality and critical judgment<br>Submition format:<br>Option 1: Artwork - Format Files: JPG/ JPEG/ GIF/ PNG<br>A.i. Usage log: Format Files: .docx/PDF<br><br>Option 2: .Create a quiz of 45- 60 multiple-choice questions<br>Notes/Requirement<br>1. Description: Student groups (5-6 students in large groups or 2-3 students in small groups)<br>a. Use AI to create multiple-choice questions from the assigned chapters<br>● Number: 20–30 questions.<br>● Level distribution:<br>Recognition: about 9–13 questions. (name, time, place, author, work, style, material...)<br>Comprehension: about 9–14 questions. (stylistic characteristics, historical-social context, meaning of work, comparison of movements...)<br>Application/Analysis: about 2–3 questions (relating the work to the historical context, analyzing the influence of style, identifying style through images, explaining why the work is typical...)<br>b. Each question must have 4 answer options, and 1 correct answer is clearly marked.<br>c. Make sure the questions:<br>● Correct knowledge, closely follow the content of the assigned chapter, assigned documents<br>● Concise, clear, reasonable answers.<br>● Images used are in the document<br>Submition format:<br>Option 1: Slides - Format Files: PPT/PDF<br>A.i. Usage log: Format Files: .docx/PDF<br>Individual: 45-60'&quot;<br>- Student must finish progress test 1 and submit the result to the lecturer in class.<br><br>Option 3: (For Constructivism Approach only): Follow lecturer's proposal</span></div>\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">Note / Ghi chú</span><span class=\"v\">A.i. Usage log: Students are encouraged to use it during their assignments. If used, an explanation must be submitted according to the following requirements: (State AI tools: Name, role, and stage of use; adhere to AI ethics and technical principles.<br>Analyze support: Specify the level of AI contribution (e.g., search, image generation, content editing, visualization).<br>Self-assess: Assess the balance between team/individual contributions and AI, ensuring humans play a central role.</span></div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"ml-en\"><h3>Sessions in the plan that mention it</h3>\n<ul><li>Session 32 — FINAL REVIEWS; Q&amp;A</li><li>Session 33 — PROGRESS TEST 1 (in 30 minutes)</li><li>Session 59 — FINAL REVIEWS; Q&amp;A</li><li>Session 60 — PROGRESS TEST 2 (in 30 minutes)</li></ul></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><h3>Buổi trong kế hoạch có nhắc tới</h3>\n<ul><li>Buổi 32 — FINAL REVIEWS; Q&amp;A</li><li>Buổi 33 — PROGRESS TEST 1 (in 30 minutes)</li><li>Buổi 59 — FINAL REVIEWS; Q&amp;A</li><li>Buổi 60 — PROGRESS TEST 2 (in 30 minutes)</li></ul></div>\n<div class=\"ml-en\"><p class=\"ghi-chu\">No practice paper for this subject in the Exam Room yet.</p></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><p class=\"ghi-chu\">Phòng thi chưa có đề luyện cho môn này.</p></div>\n<div class=\"ml-en\"><div class=\"note-ct\">📝 Exam-strategy notes and worked past papers: coming later.</div></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><div class=\"note-ct\">📝 Chiến lược làm bài và chữa đề: sẽ bổ sung sau.</div></div>"
